    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d404">

                <pb facs="0937" n="897" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v09p1/pg897"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">784A.5 MSP/2–2752:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 404<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Israel (Davis) to the Department of State</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d404-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Tel
                                Aviv</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1952-02-27T18:00:00+02:00">February 27, 1952—6
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>880. Embtel 879, Feb 27 re signing this
                    morning of agreement under Section 205 Mutual Security Act.<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d404-f2"/></p>
                <pb facs="0938" n="898" xml:id="pg898"/>
                <p>In conversation with Foreign Minister Sharett, I took occasion mention several points covered in
                        Embtel 844, Feb 20.<anchor n="3"
                        xml:id="d404-f3"/> Stressed importance to effective economic cooperation of
                    continuing to have the complete detailed info now being supplied by GOI authorities. Also reminded Foreign Minister of
                    our great interest in efforts improve Arab-Israel relations. Sharett said he appreciated importance of
                    supplying info referred to, and agreed that everything possible should be done
                    to improve Israel’s position with respect to its neighbors. Said he was glad to say GOI had recently received from Jordan sources an indication of
                    interest in improving relations with Israel. Foreign Minister Sharett plans leave tomorrow for Paris enroute
                    London where he expects remain for several weeks.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Davis</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d404-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d404-f1-content">
                <p>Repeated to Paris, London, Ankara, Beirut, Damascus, Amman, Cairo, Baghdad, and
                    Jerusalem.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d404-f2" n="2" xml:id="d404-f2-content">
                <p>Telegram 879 from Tel Aviv, Feb. 27 (884A.00 TA/2–2752), referred to the exchange
                    of notes that morning effecting an economic assistance agreement between the
                    United States and Israel relating to the relief and resettlement of refugees;
                    for the text, see 3 UST (pt. 3) 3703.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d404-f3" n="3" xml:id="d404-f3-content">
                <p>Telegram 844 from Tel Aviv, Feb. 20, referred in part to a procedure initiated on
                    Jan. 14 under which semimonthly conferences were held with officials of the
                    Ministry of Finance concerning the details of balance of payments, ordinary
                    development and defense budgets, internal and external debt positions, current
                    foreign exchange positions, and overall plans for the stabilization of the
                    Israeli economy. The telegram also referred to Technical Cooperation
                    Administration procedures for the disbursement of aid funds on the basis of
                    programs covering specific projects; and to the importance for Israel of keeping
                    its resources under constant scrutiny. (884A.00 TA/2–2052)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
